comments.body:
I found a workaround, but it would be nice if this problem could be solved more elegantly.

Since the file was being downloaded in its entirety, I added some code to ignore the EOFException.

if (responseCode == HttpStatus.SC_OK && entity != null) {
					outStream = new BufferedOutputStream(new FileOutputStream(outFilename));
					long length = entity.getContentLength();
					try {
						entity.writeTo(outStream);
					} catch (EOFException e) {
						// Sometimes we get EOFExceptions if the content length
						// wasn't specified by the server.  Ignore these but report
						// those where the content length was specified.
						if (length >= 0) {
							throw e;
						}
					}
				}
